  "step": 1,
  "note": "Order case for the same-tick throttle rule (Module.lean `sameTickThrottle`): the takeoff ramp of ModeAltHold, set_throttle_out(throttle) then D_init_controller in one tick (takeoff.cpp:83-86). Same vehicle and parameters as order-init-then-update-case.json (at rest at the origin, 1 g measured, est_accel_ef_z = -9.80665 so get_estimated_accel_D_mss = 0, hover throttle 0.5, PSC_D_ACC_FF = D = 0). Step 0 as there. Step 1 is sequenced: update_estimates (_seq 1), the supervisor's set_throttle_out(0.3) (cmd_attitude_set_throttle_out, _throttle_in = 0.3f = 0x3e99999a, _seq 2), D_init_controller (_seq 3), D_update_controller (_seq 4); ac_throttle_in, the previous tick's throttle, is 0.25. Hand prediction: D_init_controller reads get_throttle_in() = 0.3f (the call at _seq 2 precedes it), so set_integrator(-(0.3f - 0.5) - kP*(0 - 0) - FF*0) (AC_PosControl.cpp:920-922) stores 0.5 - 0.3f, exact by Sterbenz's lemma: 0.19999998807907104 = 0x3e4ccccc, within +-IMAX (0.8). D_update_controller: position, velocity and acceleration errors are 0, so P = D = 0, the integrator does not move (error 0), FF = 0; thrust_d_norm = I - hover = 0x3e4ccccc - 0.5 = -0.3f exactly (Sterbenz again), and set_throttle_out(-thrust_d_norm) gives throttle_in = 0.3f = 0x3e99999a, pc_accel_d_i = 0x3e4ccccc, pc_throttle_seq = 4 (D_update_controller's _seq). Before the rule the same step gave integrator 0.25 and throttle_in 0.25 (the previous tick's throttle, as in order-init-then-update-case.json step 1): the ramp's increment was lost every tick. The other step-1 outputs are those of order-init-then-update-case.json step 1; all were checked against the run, then recorded. Inputs added with the loiter stage (the 25 lt_ hand-over ports) are false/0: no loiter call; every previously recorded output field came out bit-identical when this file was regenerated (2026-11-18).",
